A||N||2||Darren's 87 coupe||water in the radiator||||1||
Z||000000||Darren's 87 coupe||09-06-2001||11:01 AM||||I am a new owner of an 87 Fiero coupe that my Fater in Law gave me.  He kept it in great condition.  It was his daily driver up until about 2 years ago when it got oil in the radiator.  He decided not to mess with it anymore and I saved it from going to the scrap yard.  I am reading as much as I can on Fieros and was hoping that someone could help me out as to the problem.  What is causing the oil in the radiator and what could fix it?  I have some car knowledge and can do some myself.  Tell me if you think this is a fairly easy repair, or should I take it to a professional?||||reg||1
Z||000001||Nashco||09-06-2001||11:36 AM||||Sounds like a probable bad head gasket or cracked head.  Hard to say either way without tearing it apart.  If you have a service manual, a lot of tools, and a torque wrench, you could tackle the job alone, but it is advisable to have a pro do it if you've never taken a head off.  It's not too intense of a job, just bolt on/off, but risk of messing up is pretty high in that area.  Others will have more to add, I'm sure.<P>Bryce<BR>88 GT||||reg||1
Z||000002||theogre||09-06-2001||07:13 PM||||If it's been messed up for that long, you'd be better off finding another motor. These motors are used in several GM cars. Grand Am and Olds Cutlass Calaiss for a couple... The motors are the same, you'll need to swap pulleys and brackets but that's allot easier and likely cheaper than the work that head, and maybe the block, probably needs now.<P>You can probably find a decent used motor for $200-300 at many salvage yards.<P>And yes, the motor can come out the top. It's easier if you yank the motor and tranny together, especially with a manual tranny. then you don't have to fight under the car with the starter mounting and bell housing clearance. (The clutch takes up a bunch of space. Unlike the Torque converter which gets left in the tranny when the engine comes out.)<P>If it's a stick I'd do the clutch while it's out.||||reg||1
